1510377.steps:
1. Navigate to Network/Routing page, click tab "Route Policies", switch to IPv4 view page;
2. Click Add button to add a new route policy, then an add route policy dialog box opens;
3. Check all fields on this dialog box, src any, destination Network 20.1.1.0/24, select radio button "Multi-Path Route";
4. Select "Gateway Number:" as 4, configure interface and gateway as X2 and X2 gateway, configure interface2 and gateway2 as X3 and X3 gateway, configure interface3 and gateway3 as X4 and X4 gateway, configure interface4 and gateway4 as X5 and X5 gateway, metric, click ok button.
5. Run continuous and large traffic to the destination, check connection monitor;
6. Shutdown interface X2, and then shutdown X3, and then shutdown X4, and then shutdown X5, check traffic and connection cache monitor.
7. No shutdown(up) interface X2, check traffic and connection cache monitor.
8. UP interface X3, check traffic and connection cache monitor.
9. UP interface X4, check traffic and connection cache monitor.
10. UP interface X5, check traffic and connection cache monitor.

